1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
[Original electronic instrumental music]
Why does waiting explode before a system is full?

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,000
One barista finishes one order a minute, on average.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:21,000
But arrivals and service times vary.
Little rushes make a queue.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:29,000
At 50% busy, this model predicts
a 1-minute average wait.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:39,000
At 90% busy, the average wait is
9 minutes—before service.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:49,000
In this random queue model,
waiting rises nonlinearly.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Spare capacity absorbs the unexpected
instead of passing it on as delay.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Leave room for the rush.
